      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "The sooner you allow users to create assets, the sooner you'll get some stronger goods to sell.   Keeping the system restricted to corporate partners who pay you enough money is going to gradually alienate you from your community.  Let the creatives work and take your cut from that rather than trying to control the income stream at heavily reduced levels.   Cheaper goods mean that people buy things more often, including things they might not even use.  Steam shows us every day why this works.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
